--[[
	The values the author ships: the "def" of every option in his MCM tables, carried
	through the same arithmetic his appliers use. A drop-down list takes the NAME of its
	entry, which is how the console command of a list is written.

	This exists because the stock trackbar answers "set_default_value" with the MIDDLE OF
	ITS RANGE ( xrGame\ui\UITrackBar.cpp, OnMessage ). That is Call of Pripyat's own code and
	it is shared with the stock defaults buttons, so it stays as it is - but a midpoint is not
	a default.

	OnBtnSSFXReset in ui_mm_opt_main.script writes these to the console and then re-reads the
	page from it, the same pattern OnBtnKeybDefault uses for the key bindings.

	The last section is not the author's: those are engine settings, and their value is the
	one the engine itself starts with.

	Generated by _ssfx_work\menu_page_build.py - run it again rather than editing here.
--]]

